<v Josh Johnson>Have you ever been-- OK, have you ever been in a bar, and then you see a fight brew-- you can smell it brewing. And then you're also like, I think if you had, like, punched your dad years ago, none of this would be happening right now. Like, if you had just had one good row with him, this would be a quiet evening, right?
<v Josh Johnson>你有没有——好的，你有没有在酒吧里，看到架势正在酝酿——你能闻到它在酝酿。然后你也会想，我觉得如果你几年前打了你爸爸，现在这一切都不会发生了。就像，如果你和他吵过一架，现在会是个安静的夜晚，对吧？

00:41:55.550 --> 00:42:00.680
<v Josh Johnson>[LAUGHTER]
<v Josh Johnson>[笑声]

00:42:00.680 --> 00:42:29.210
<v Josh Johnson>And, uh, they were going at each other. And some of it was punching. Some of it was kicking. Now, the guy that was, like, on the bigger side and muscular-- he really knew his way around. Like, he was even doing the hop of someone who knows how to fight. You know that little light-foot hop where you're like, they're about to get into it. OK. And then, there was one moment-- because I walked out of this bar, because I was doing a show, like a bar show with my friends, and then we were all walking out. And we all saw this, like, happening.
<v Josh Johnson>他们在那互相攻击。有一些是拳击。有一些是踢腿。现在，那个大块头且肌肉发达的家伙——他真的很懂行。他甚至摆出了懂打架人的那种弹跳。你知道那种轻盈的弹跳吗，当你是的时候，他们快要动真格了。好的。然后，有一个瞬间——因为我走出了这个酒吧，因为我在做演出，和我朋友们的一个酒吧演出，然后我们都走出来。我们都看到这事正在发生。

